{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1482942-deviant-factions-within-a-conspiracy-node","id":1482942,"title":"[Deviant] Factions within a Conspiracy Node","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-03T09:52:36-07:00","id":1482942,"title":"[Deviant] Factions within a Conspiracy Node","content":"Let's say that the Hierarchical Node of a Conspiracy is a council of sorts, like a board of directors. They're essentially a group of NPCs with a mutual interest, or an &quot;alliance&quot;, but they may each have their own goals and agenda and there may be different &quot;factions&quot; within the council.<br /> Normally everything runs smoothly in the Conspiracy but Renegade action might cause conflict within the council.<br /> <br /> What would be the best way to frame these factions within the council? Would that count as two separate Hierarchical Nodes or a single one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T13:23:00-07:00","id":1482965,"title":"","content":"Not every conspiracy action has to be a Conspiracy Action, which models mass action and organizational effort the group puts forth.<br /> <br /> If you're just looking at internal strife, you might simply leave it as one hierarchical node whose infighting could change the conspiracy's priorities from action to action. You might do something like give one hierarchical node two linchpins and enable it to continue functioning even if one is taken out, or give it an Icon representing flexibility that allows the conspiracy to act on alternate Principles and Anchors based on which faction is ascendant. A conspiracy with internal strife is a good candidate for Going Deeper (p. 234), revealing on the destruction of the conspiracy the rise of an Inheritor conspiracy from the ashes or a Master conspiracy that had been manipulating it through the rogue faction.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you could be looking at multiple conspiracies, perhaps conspiracies that share some of their nodes in common, or engaging in subversion of each others' structure (p. 232).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T09:47:16-07:00","id":1483146,"title":"","content":"Don\u2019t forget about Conditions like Coup d\u2019etat and Heresy. I don\u2019t know if these were included in Deviant, but Geist and Mummy both have conditions to reflect various setbacks and internal strife.<br /> <br /> As Loserman suggested, I\u2019d probably model this as one Node with rapidly changing priorities, and probably random penalties or paralysis, as the infighting effectively acts as a \u201cblock someone else\u2019s social merits\u201d maneuver.<br /> <br /> In that kind of organization, though, there will usually be strong section heads answering to the council. When orders from up top get inconsistent, the people in charge of execution might pick winners, force a compromise, or strike off on their own. <br /> That, or each Council Member is a section head (thinking of the various gang leaders under Kingpin, in the Netflix Daredevil). In which case, each branch would operate just fine, but absent any resources or coordination with the others (causing huge problems) leading up to dissolving into separate conspiracies.<br /> Either of those situations might have multiple nodes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}